Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:18:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Contact page writes and people settings (the frontend's 14
 Oct 14:10Z, items 1 and 2)

Misho asked the frontend to send the routes its remaining design pages
need. Items 1 and 2, wrapping what the chat tools already do:

- the contact page's own facts by id: list, add (a note), correct,
  forget; an exclusion taken back by id; remove from the network; mark
  as passed away. `:id` is the existing contact id; a contact that is not
  the person's own is 404 and nothing is written. Facts and exclusions on
  GET /contacts/:id now carry their ids.
- GET /profile/people-settings: the person's exclusions (with a contact
  id and name) and topic boundaries (by topic), each with an id;
  DELETE /profile/boundaries/:id takes a topic back.

Not built (FOR_FRONTEND says why): labels and warmth writes, an exclusion
by goal id, and a per-contact boundary each need a product decision.

